        # Step help/json handling: if any segment has --help/--json-usage, original resolves that step and shows its help before checking other steps after unknown option validations in that segment. We'll handle in segment execution for that step, but structural unknown/first/last validations happen before? For `info --help` in a pipeline with read first, help succeeded. For a pipeline consisting only `info --help`, script gave step help (tested) despite info not generation/final alone. So scan for help token in any segment after unknown step name check for segments up to that segment, before first/last validations.
